        "original_id": "501e31ca-9845-5603-a6b4-68747e6b2eec",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game\n- Places: BB&T Center, Sunrise, Florida\n- Organizations: Florida Panthers, National Hockey League\n- Topics: 2002–03 Florida Panthers season\n\nFacts:\n- BB&T Center in Sunrise, Florida, was completed in 1998 at a cost of US$185 million and was financed almost entirely with public funds.\n- BB&T Center in Sunrise, Florida, has 70 suites and 2,623 club seats.\n- The 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game took place on February 2, 2003, during the 2002–03 NHL season.\n- The 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game was held at the Office Depot Center in Sunrise, Florida, which was the home arena of the Florida Panthers.\n- BB&T Center in Sunrise, Florida, was previously known as the National Car Rental Center, Office Depot Center, and BankAtlantic Center.\n- During the 2002–03 Florida Panthers season, the Florida Panthers did not make the playoffs.\n- During the 2002–03 Florida Panthers season, the Florida Panthers hosted the 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
